{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n22 modules under `tests/unit/metrics/` (13 pairs), `tests/unit/workflow/` (3 pairs) and `tests/unit/reconciler/` (6 pairs: 2 in `diffing/`, 3 in `state/`, 1 at the package root) have a `<name>_heldout.py` twin. Once both oracles have been reviewed the split only doubles module count, duplicates identical helper definitions, and makes every rename touch two files. Across these 22 pairs no test-function name collides; 7 pairs carry helper/fixture/class definitions with differing bodies (14 definitions in all) and every other colliding definition is identical. The pair list with per-pair rename sets, filtered from enumeration (2) of the test-suite epic's first comment, is itemised in this ticket's first comment. Paths are stated at their post-rename name: the reconciler epic (friended-brainsick-degus) rename has LANDED, so `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` no longer exists and the modules live under `tests/unit/reconciler/`. All counts and paths in this plan were re-measured on origin/main 7927904a0 by listing `tests/unit/{metrics,workflow,reconciler}/` and AST-diffing every pair's top-level definitions, not sampled.\n\n## Approach\nDirectories: `tests/unit/metrics/`, `tests/unit/workflow/`, `tests/unit/reconciler/` — 22 pairs (13 metrics, 3 workflow, 6 reconciler — 2 in `diffing/`, 3 in `state/`, 1 at the package root). **14 definition renames over 7 pairs**, enumerated so the set does not have to be re-derived: `metrics/test_registry` (`_spec`); `metrics/test_event_metrics` (`_write_event`, `_ticket`); `metrics/test_git_metrics` (`_oracle_write_cap`); `metrics/test_sidecar_metrics` (`_review`, `_write`); `workflow/test_gate_error_sidecar` (`_OutageRunner`, `_gate_errors`); `reconciler/state/test_backend_scalar_surface` (`_backend`); `reconciler/diffing/test_canonical_outbound_equivalence` (`_jira`, `backend`, `_emit`, `_StubBindingStore`, `_ticket`). `reconciler/diffing/test_canonical_link_diff` was previously listed as a rename and is NOT one: its shared definitions are byte-identical, so it dedupes with no rename. For each pair: `cat` the held-out module into the base under a `# ── held-out oracles (merged from <name>_heldout.py) ──` divider; keep the base module docstring and append the held-out docstring's \"what it proves\" paragraph; dedupe identical definitions (`pytestmark` counts here — keep the base copy); rename differing definitions and repoint their callers; `git rm` the held-out file. Rename rule: suffix the HELD-OUT definition `_heldout` (e.g. `_load_heldout`) and repoint its callers; keep the base copy of identical definitions. The autouse fixture `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_backend_scalar_surface{,_heldout}.py::_clean` has identical bodies: the merge keeps the base copy, so the base mechanism key survives and the held-out key buckets `stale`. No test body changes.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: the 22 base modules under `tests/unit/metrics/`, `tests/unit/workflow/` and `tests/unit/reconciler/` named in the first comment and their 22 `_heldout` twins. Out of scope: the `tests/unit/` root pairs (S1), `tests/interfaces/` and `tests/integration/` (S3), `tests/scripts/` (S4), the 78 unpaired held-out renames (S5), `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`, every file under `src/`, and any test body change.\n\n`tests/unit/review_bot/` was flagged as possibly unclaimed by any story in this epic. It is not: all 3 of its `_heldout` modules are **unpaired**, so they belong to `b721-6c6d`'s unpaired-rename pass, whose scope claims the 55 unpaired modules under `tests/unit/` *including its subpackages*. Nothing is added to this story.\n\n## Testing\nPer pair: `pytest --collect-only -q <base> <heldout>` before and `pytest --collect-only -q <base>` after — counts equal (both recorded on this ticket); `pytest <base>` green. `make test` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Zero paired twins remain in these directories: for each of the 22 pairs `git ls-files <base>_heldout.py` prints nothing (the unpaired `_heldout` modules in these directories are untouched here and renamed in S5).\n- [ ] Per-pair node counts reconcile: each merged base collects exactly the sum of the two prior counts, from the before/after `pytest --collect-only -q` runs recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` **exits 0**; the held-out `_clean` autouse key of `test_backend_scalar_surface_heldout.py` buckets `stale`, which `--check` accepts (`scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py:51-57`), and `--update-stale` is not run. AMENDED: this criterion previously also required the `--check` summary to report `new=0`, which is unreachable and unrelated to this story's work — `new=N` counts marker-admitted entries, so an already-clean tree reports a nonzero `new` and still exits 0. Exit 0 is the gate's pass signal. Root cause: bug `6f24-3d47-b251-4905`, whose fix has landed in `AGENTS.md` and `rebar explain plan`.\n- [ ] `make verify` green."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793479196132358001,"uuid":"cf765455-bd58-40de-8632-c9730224ee2d"}